/target
# mkdocs build output (generated by `mkdocs build`; the Pages workflow builds it in CI)
/site
# cargo-fuzz build output and evolved corpora/crash artifacts (standalone workspace).
# Cargo.lock is intentionally committed (not ignored) so the scheduled Fuzz
# workflow builds a reproducible, pinned dependency graph instead of fresh-
# resolving each run — a fresh resolution once drifted into a panicking
# transitive (jiff-core 0.1.0), turning the weekly fuzz red on a graph the rest
# of CI never compiles.
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/corpus
/fuzz/artifacts
# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
